# Code Style and Quality - C# and .NET

## Core Values
- **Consistency**: Follow existing patterns in the codebase
- **Clarity**: Code should be self-documenting when possible
- **Maintainability**: Future developers (including yourself) should understand the code easily
- **Simplicity**: Prefer simple, obvious solutions over clever tricks

## File Organization

### Standard File Structure
```csharp
using Godot;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public partial class EnemyController : Node2D
{
    // 1. Documentation (if needed)
    /// <summary>
    /// Controls enemy behavior, including movement and attack patterns.
    /// Integrates with EventBus for communication and EntityFactory for spawning.
    /// </summary>

    // 2. Signals (grouped logically)
    [Signal] public delegate void HealthChangedEventHandler(int newHealth, int oldHealth);
    [Signal] public delegate void DefeatedEventHandler(int enemyId, Vector2 position);
    [Signal] public delegate void PhaseChangedEventHandler(int phaseNumber);

    // 3. Enums
    public enum State
    {
        Idle,
        Moving,
        Attacking,
        Dying,
    }

    // 4. Constants
    private const int MaxHealth = 100;
    private const float AttackRange = 150.0f;
    private const float MovementSpeed = 100.0f;

    // 5. Export variables (grouped by category)
    [ExportGroup("Stats")]
    [Export] public int MaxHealth { get; set; } = 100;
    [Export] public int Damage { get; set; } = 10;

    [ExportGroup("Behavior")]
    [Export] public string MovementPattern { get; set; } = "straight";
    [Export] public float AttackCooldown { get; set; } = 2.0f;

    // 6. Public properties
    public int Health { get; set; } = 100;
    public State CurrentState { get; set; } = State.Idle;

    // 7. Private fields (underscore prefix)
    private Vector2 _velocity = Vector2.Zero;
    private Node2D _target;
    private Player _cachedPlayer;

    // 8. Built-in virtual methods (in this order)
    public override void _Ready()
    {
        // Initialization
    }

    public override void _Process(double delta)
    {
        // Game logic
    }

    public override void _PhysicsProcess(double delta)
    {
        // Physics logic
    }

    public override void _Input(InputEvent @event)
    {
        // Input handling
    }

    // 9. Public methods
    public void TakeDamage(int amount)
    {
        // Implementation
    }

    public void SetTarget(Node2D target)
    {
        // Implementation
    }

    // 10. Private methods (underscore prefix)
    private void UpdateMovement(double delta)
    {
        // Implementation
    }

    private void HandleDeath()
    {
        // Implementation
    }

    // 11. Signal handlers (grouped at end)
    private void OnHealthDepleted()
    {
        // Implementation
    }

    private void OnPlayerDetected(Player player)
    {
        // Implementation
    }
}
```

## Naming Conventions

### Variables and Properties
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Descriptive, typed, PascalCase for public, camelCase for private
public int PlayerHealth { get; set; } = 100;
public float MovementSpeed { get; set; } = 150.0f;
public bool IsInvulnerable { get; set; } = false;
public List<Enemy> EnemyList { get; set; } = new();
public Vector2 TargetPosition { get; set; } = Vector2.Zero;

// Private fields with underscore prefix
private int _internalState = 0;
private Node _cachedReference;

// ❌ BAD: Vague, untyped, or wrong casing
public var hp; // What type? Player or enemy HP?
public var spd; // Abbreviation unclear
public List<Enemy> enemyList; // Wrong casing (camelCase for public)
private int _publicVar; // Underscore but actually public
```

### Methods
```csharp
// ✅ GOOD: Verb-based, descriptive, typed
public float CalculateDamageMultiplier(int baseDamage, float rank)
{
    return baseDamage * (1.0f + rank * 0.1f);
}

public Enemy SpawnEnemyAtPosition(string templateId, Vector2 position)
{
    return EntityFactory.SpawnEnemy(templateId, position, Vector2.Down);
}

public bool IsInAttackRange(Node2D target)
{
    return GlobalPosition.DistanceSquaredTo(target.GlobalPosition) < AttackRange * AttackRange;
}

// Private methods with underscore
private void InternalUpdateLogic()
{
    // Implementation
}

// ❌ BAD: Vague names, no types
public void Update() // Update what?
{
    // Implementation
}

public object Calc(object x, object y) // Calculate what? Returns what?
{
    return x; // What is this?
}

public void attackEnemy() // Wrong casing
{
    // Implementation
}
```

